#import "../lib.typ": *

#section(
  exercise([
    #drill-heading(107)

    This is a most excellent word to practice at this stage of the work. It is a good movement-developer. Give close attention to size, general appearance, and space between letters, and guard against irregular movement. Keep the hand well up in front of the eyes and drive the pen lightly.
    Write a half page of the copy and then make a careful study of your work.
    Try to write each line better than the preceding. Three words should be
    written to the line.
  ], lines: 6, slots: 2, examples: ("drill-107", "drill-107")),
  exercise([
    #drill-heading(108)

    Work faithfully on every letter. Repeat the forms over and over until
    decided improvement can be seen. Make frequent comparisons. Study length,
    breadth, curves and connections closely.

    #instruction[Write fifty F's, thirty-five H's, thirty-five K's, thirty-five M's, and forty N's in 60 seconds.]
  ], lines: 9, slots: 4, examples: ("drill-108", "drill-108-2", "drill-108-3", "drill-108-4", "drill-108-5")),
  exercise([
    #drill-heading(109)

    *Points to Observe*—Capital Q is the enlarged form of figure two. The last parts of U, V, and W are shorter than the other parts, and the first strokes in U and V are exactly alike. In capital W, check the motion a little at the base line in the first main downward stroke, as this will aid in the construction of the last part.

    #instruction[Write sixty Q's, forty-five U's, fifty-five V's, and forty W's in 60 seconds.]
  ], lines: 8, slots: 2, examples: ("drill-109", "drill-109-2", "drill-109-3", "drill-109-4")),
  exercise([
    #drill-heading(110)

    Practice this compact oval as a beginning drill. Make it between two ruled lines, carry the pen lightly and see how many you can make in one row, with one dip of ink.
  ], lines: 6, examples: ("drill-110", "drill-110")),
  exercise([
    #drill-heading(111)

    Study and compare as you practice.

    At this point it would be a good plan to review all the essential work of
    the preceding lessons. From one to two weeks should be spent in such
    practice.

    #instruction[Write thirty-five X's, forty Y's, and fifty Z's in 60 seconds.]
  ], lines: 7, slots: 6, examples: ("drill-111", "drill-111-2", "drill-111-3")),
)
